Vendored third-party code keeps its own licence, which travels beside it:

  Lua 5.4, by Lua.org / PUC-Rio, MIT
      lua/upstream/, and the notice is at the bottom of lua.h

  stb_truetype.h, stb_image.h and stb_image_write.h, by Sean Barrett, MIT or public domain
      runtime/upstream/stb/, notice at the bottom of each header,
      pointed at by LICENSE.stb beside them, which also records the
      version and commit each was taken from

  miniz 3.0.2, by Rich Geldreich, RAD Game Tools and Valve Software, MIT
      runtime/upstream/miniz/LICENSE; its deflater makes the zips Tracker
      compresses, and README.md beside it says how it is built

  musl's maths functions, by Rich Felker and others, MIT
      runtime/upstream/musl-math/COPYRIGHT, which also lists the other
      permissive notices parts of musl carry; the vendoring is recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it

  TinyGL, by Fabrice Bellard and erysdren, MIT
      runtime/upstream/tinygl/COPYING, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it

  NetSurf's libraries, by J-M Bell and the NetSurf Browser Project, MIT
      runtime/upstream/netsurf/: libcss, libdom, libhubbub, libparserutils,
      libsvgtiny and libwapcaplet, each under the COPYING file in its own
      directory

  expat 2.8.5, by the Thai Open Source Software Center, Clark Cooper and
      the Expat maintainers, MIT
      runtime/upstream/expat/COPYING, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it

  minimp3, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minimp3/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minimp3.h

  minih264, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minih264/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minih264e.h

  minimp4, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minimp4/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minimp4.h

  ufbx, by Samuli Raivio, MIT or public domain
      runtime/upstream/ufbx/LICENSE, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it

  luacheck, by Peter Melnichenko and contributors, MIT
      runtime/upstream/luacheck/LICENSE, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it; and the SHA-1 it carries, under
      src/luacheck/vendor/sha1/LICENSE

  BearSSL 0.6, by Thomas Pornin, MIT
      runtime/upstream/bearssl/LICENSE.txt, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it; the TLS Kit's protocol, and its brssl
      tool built on the Mac to turn the roots below into trust anchors

  LakeSnes, by angelo_wf and contributors, the CX4 by dink, MIT
      runtime/upstream/lakesnes/LICENSE.txt, with the vendoring recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it. Not in the system's image: `make
      apps` links it into snes.elf, installed in /Home/Apps/SNES

  intel-gpu-tools' GPGPU fill kernel, by Intel Corporation, MIT
      The ten instructions in user/drivers/display/intelgpu_fill.h, the
      first program Kosmos runs on the M700's execution units, from
      igt-gpu-tools 2.6's lib/gpgpu_fill.c, credited there

  i915's starting render state for generation 9, by Intel Corporation, MIT
      user/drivers/display/intelgpu_renderstate.h, from Linux 6.12's
      drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/gen9_renderstate.c, credited there

  intel-gpu-tools' render copy for generation 9, by Intel Corporation, MIT
      user/drivers/display/intelgpu_render.h and intelgpu_blend.h - its
      pixel shader, and the batches tools/render_batch.c writes after
      lib/rendercopy_gen9.c with
      the genxml packers igt-gpu-tools 2.6 generates - credited there

  The fonts
      assets/fonts/, each under the LICENSE file beside it. A font
      whose licence is not beside it is not committed, and the build
      says so when it finds one.

  IBM Plex Sans JP, KR, SC and TC, by IBM, SIL Open Font License 1.1
      Not in the tree or the system's image: tools/fetch_fonts.py
      fetches them, held to their sums, and `make install-apps` and a
      stick's /Home put them in /Home/Fonts with the licence beside
      them, where a process reads one the first time a character needs it

  Hyphenation patterns from the hyph-utf8 package
      assets/hyphenation/: American English by Gerard D.C. Kuiken, which
      may be copied with or without changes provided its notice is kept,
      and Spanish by Javier Bezos and CervanTeX, MIT; each language's terms
      in the LICENSE file beside it, and where they came from in
      README.kosmos.md

  Lucide's icons, by Lucide Icons and Contributors, ISC
      assets/icons/lucide/, under the LICENSE beside them, which also
      gives the MIT terms of the icons derived from Feather, by Cole
      Bemis; the vendoring is recorded in README.kosmos.md, and the line
      icons rendered from them into assets/icons/line/ carry the same terms

  The Haiku icons, by Haiku, Inc., MIT
      assets/icons/, under the LICENSE beside them. The Haiku logo and
      leaf are Haiku, Inc.'s trademarks, and neither is among them

  Mozilla's root certificates, as curl publishes them, MPL 2.0
      assets/ca/cacert.pem, the roots the TLS Kit trusts; where it came
      from, its hash and its licence are in the README beside it

  The filter lists, by The EasyList authors and Fanboy
      assets/filters/: EasyList and EasyPrivacy under the GPL version 3
      or CC BY-SA 3.0, EasyList Cookie under CC BY 3.0, unmodified, and
      converted into WebKit's rules when the image is built; where each
      came from and its hash are in the README beside them. In images
      that carry WebKit only

  "Dam", the Wikipedia article, by its contributors, CC BY-SA 4.0
      assets/www/dam.html, as en.wikipedia.org served it on 30 September
      2026 to the browser's User-Agent, unmodified: the browser's standing
      large page. The article's history names its authors

  The wallpapers, twelve abstract pictures chosen by Diego Cibils
      assets/wallpapers/, as he gave them, at their own resolutions, from
      WallpaperAccess for personal use; each one's id there is in the
      README. In `FULL=1` images only

  Project Wycheproof's test vectors, by Google and C2SP, Apache 2.0
      tools/vectors/wycheproof/, under the LICENSE beside them, the commit
      and each file's hash in the README there. Not in the system's
      image: the Crypto Kit's test is held to them on the Mac

  libc++, libc++abi and libunwind, by the LLVM project, Apache 2.0 + LLVM Exceptions
      runtime/upstream/llvm/, in LICENSE.TXT, with the vendoring recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it: LLVM 23.1.2, less its tests, and the
      120 files of LLVM's libc libc++ includes. The C++ an image carries
      stands on them; the system's image carries none yet

  ICU 79.1, by Unicode, Inc. and others, Unicode License v3
      Not in the tree: tools/icu_build.py fetches icu4c-79.1 and its data,
      held to their sums (docs/w4.md), and the terms are the LICENSE in
      that tarball, which also lists the third-party notices parts of ICU
      carry. Not in the system's image: `make apps` links it into the
      images that need it, jsc.elf among them, installed in /Home/Apps/JSC

  zlib 1.4, by Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler, the zlib License
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches the release, held to
      GitHub's digest (docs/w5.md W5a); the terms are at the top of zlib.h.
      Not in the system's image: only picturetest.elf, W5a's test, links it

  libpng 1.6.59, by the PNG Reference Library Authors, PNG Reference
      Library License version 2
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the release tag's commit (W5a);
      the terms are the LICENSE in the release. Only picturetest.elf

  libjpeg-turbo 3.2.1, by the libjpeg-turbo Project and the Independent
      JPEG Group, the IJG License and a BSD-style licence
      Not in the tree: fetched and held to GitHub's digest (W5a); the terms
      are LICENSE.md and README.ijg in the release. Only picturetest.elf

  libwebp 1.6.0, by Google LLC, a BSD-style licence
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the release tag's commit (W5a);
      the terms are COPYING and PATENTS in the release. Only picturetest.elf

  FreeType 2.15.0, by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, Werner Lemberg and
      the FreeType Project, the FreeType License (FTL), chosen of its two
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the release tag's commit (W5b);
      the terms are LICENSE.TXT and docs/FTL.TXT in the release. Only
      texttest.elf, W5b's test, links it

  HarfBuzz 15.1.0, by Behdad Esfahbod and the HarfBuzz authors, the
      Old MIT licence
      Not in the tree: fetched and held to GitHub's digest (W5b); the terms
      are COPYING in the release. Only texttest.elf

  SQLite 3.54.1, by D. Richard Hipp and the SQLite developers, in the
      public domain
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches the amalgamation and the
      source tree, held to sqlite.org's SHA3-256 (docs/w5.md W5c); the
      dedication is at the top of sqlite3.c. Only sqltest.elf, W5c's
      test, links it

  libxml2 2.15.4, by Daniel Veillard and the libxml2 contributors, under
      the MIT licence
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches GNOME's release, held to
      its SHA-256 (docs/w5.md W5c); the notice is its Copyright file. Only
      xmltest.elf, W5c's test, links it

  libpsl 0.23.3, by Tim Rühsen and the libpsl contributors, under the MIT
      licence, with Chromium's DAFSA lookup under a BSD licence
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches its release, held to
      GitHub's SHA-256 (docs/w5.md W5c); the notices are its COPYING and
      src/LICENSE.chromium. Only xmltest.elf links it

  OpenSSL 4.1.0, by the OpenSSL Project Authors, under the Apache License
      2.0
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches its release, held to
      GitHub's SHA-256 (docs/w5.md W5d); the terms are its LICENSE.txt.
      Only ssltest.elf, W5d's test, links it

  LLVM 23.1.2's own libraries, by the LLVM project, Apache 2.0 + LLVM
      Exceptions
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches its release, held to
      GitHub's SHA-256 (docs/gpu3d.md G1), and tools/llvm_build.py applies
      runtime/patches/llvm/ as it builds; the terms are its LICENSE.TXT.
      Only llvmtest.elf, G1's test, links it

  curl 8.23.0, by Daniel Stenberg and the curl contributors, under the curl
      licence, MIT-style
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches its release, held to
      GitHub's SHA-256 (docs/w5.md W5d); the terms are its COPYING. Only
      curltest.elf, W5d's test, links it

  nghttp2 1.71.0, by Tatsuhiro Tsujikawa and the nghttp2 contributors,
      under the MIT licence
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches its release, held to
      GitHub's SHA-256 (docs/w5.md); the terms are its COPYING. Its library
      only, linked with curl: curltest.elf and JetSki's WebKit, for HTTP/2

  Brotli 1.2.1, by the Brotli authors, under the MIT
      licence
      Not in the tree: tools/upstream.py fetches it by git at the release's
      commit (docs/w5.md W5f); the terms are its LICENSE. Linked by the
      images that read WOFF2 fonts and HTTP's `br`, JetSki's among them

  WOFF2 1.0.2, by the WOFF2 authors, under the MIT licence
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the tag's commit (W5f); the terms
      are its LICENSE. Linked by JetSki's image, for a site's own fonts

  dav1d 1.5.4, by VideoLAN and the dav1d authors, a BSD 2-clause licence
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the tag's commit (W5f); the terms
      are its COPYING. Linked by the images that decode AV1 - AVIF's
      pictures and the Media Kit's video

  libavif 1.4.2, by Joe Drago and the libavif authors, a BSD 2-clause
      licence
      Not in the tree: fetched by git at the tag's commit (W5f); the terms
      are its LICENSE. Linked by JetSki's image, for AVIF pictures

  Skia, as WebKitGTK 2.54.2 carries it (milestone 154), by Google LLC and
      the Skia authors, a BSD-style licence
      Not in the tree: tools/webkit_build.py fetches WebKit's release
      (docs/w4.md) and builds Source/ThirdParty/skia with
      runtime/patches/webkit/0012-skia-on-kosmos.patch applied (docs/w5.md
      W5e); the terms are Source/ThirdParty/skia/LICENSE. Only
      skiatest.elf, W5e's test, links it

None of those are modified in place. Changes to them are build steps, so
what is in this tree is what their authors released.

Seven more are copyleft: three under the GPL, and FFmpeg's decoder,
libsmb2, TinyCC and WebKit's JavaScriptCore under the LGPL. Nothing here is linked dynamically - whatever is compiled into an
image is linked into it - so an image carrying any GPL one is a combined
work under the GPL as a whole. Kosmos's own sources stay MIT either way.

  NetSurf's layout engine, by the NetSurf Browser Project, GPLv2
      runtime/upstream/netsurf/netsurf/, in COPYING, with the vendoring
      recorded in README.kosmos.md beside it: NetSurf 3.11's box tree,
      layout, tables, flex, box drawing, forms and its text-entry widget,
      unmodified but for one header patched as it is built. In the browser,
      which the system's image carries when it is built with the web kit
      (`make qemu`'s default), so that image is a GPLv2 work.

  FFmpeg's H.264 decoder, by the FFmpeg developers, LGPL 2.1 or later
      runtime/upstream/ffmpeg/, in COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and LICENSE.md, with
      the vendoring recorded in README.kosmos.md beside it: the 95 files
      the H.264 Kit's entry points reach, unmodified. Built by default
      (`FULL=1`) and left out of `make FULL=0`, `make test` and
      `make bench`. Every source in this tree is public, so the image can
      be relinked against a changed FFmpeg, which is what the LGPL asks
      of a static link.

  libsmb2, by Ronnie Sahlberg and its contributors, LGPL 2.1 or later
      runtime/upstream/libsmb2/, in COPYING and LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt, with
      the vendoring recorded in README.kosmos.md beside it: SMB 2 and 3 for
      network file sharing (docs/sharing.md), unmodified. In no image yet -
      built only on the Mac, for its tests against Samba - and when it is,
      as FFmpeg is: every source public, so the image can be relinked.

  TinyCC, by Fabrice Bellard and its contributors, LGPL 2.1
      runtime/upstream/tinycc/, in COPYING, with the vendoring recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it; Kosmos's layout is a patch applied at
      the build. Not in the system's image yet: built on the Mac, where it
      links the test kit `make apps` makes

  WebKit's JavaScriptCore, WTF and bmalloc, by Apple Inc. and the WebKit
      contributors, LGPL 2 or later, and BSD for much of it
      Not in the tree: tools/webkit_build.py fetches WebKitGTK 2.54.2, held
      to its sum (docs/w4.md), and applies runtime/patches/webkit/ as it
      builds, so what is changed is a file anybody can read; the terms are
      each source file's own notice and Source/JavaScriptCore/COPYING.LIB.
      Not in the system's image: `make apps` links it into jsc.elf,
      installed in /Home/Apps/JSC beside jsc.lua. The release is public and
      so are the patches, so the image can be relinked against a changed
      JavaScriptCore, which is what the LGPL asks of a static link.

  WebKit's WebCore and PAL, by Apple Inc. and the WebKit contributors, LGPL
      2 or later, and BSD for much of it
      Not in the tree: the same release, with 89 files laid over it from
      WebKit's git at the release's commit (tools/upstream.py, docs/w6.md),
      and the port's own files from runtime/ports/webkit/. Not in the
      system's image: `make apps` links it into webcoretest.elf, the test
      of it (docs/w6.md W6b). The same terms as JavaScriptCore's above, and
      the same answer to the LGPL's static link.

  doomgeneric, id Software's Doom by way of Chocolate Doom, GPLv2
      runtime/upstream/doom/, in LICENSE.doomgeneric. Not in the system's
      image in any build: `make apps` links it into doom.elf, Doom's own
      image, installed in /Home/Apps/Doom beside doom.lua, and that image
      is the GPLv2 work.

  Chocolate Quake, by id Software, Henrique Barateli and others, GPL
      runtime/upstream/quake/, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it. Every source file carries id's
      "version 2, or any later version" notice, and the project's own
      LICENSE file is version 3. Not in the system's image in any build:
      `make apps` links it into quake.elf, Quake's own image, installed
      in /Home/Apps/Quake beside quake.lua, and that image is the GPL
      work.
